    "customfield_12313320": "<div style='font-weight:bold;color:red;text-align:center'>This project has a <a href=\"https://lucene.apache.org/core/discussion.html\">user mailing list and an IRC channel</a> for support. If you are looking for support, or if you are not sure whether the behavior that you are observing is expected or not, please discuss it there first.</div>",
    "customfield_12314134": null,
    "duedate": null,
    "customfield_12314132": null,
    "customfield_12314131": null,
    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12381579/comment/12539188",
          "id": "12539188",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Attaching patch.  Here's the approach I took:\n- change makeStopSet return a CharArraySet\n- make CharArraySet a real Set (plus many other small changes)\n  - the Iterator returns Strings for backward compatibility with people that\n   expect a Set<String>\n- StopFilter constructor to directly use Set if instanceof CharArraySet\n\nAll tests pass.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2007-10-31T21:07:15.034+0000",
          "updated": "2007-10-31T21:07:15.034+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12381579/comment/12539273",
          "id": "12539273",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=hossman",
            "name": "hossman",
            "key": "hossman",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247"
            },
            "displayName": "Chris M. Hostetter",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Phoenix"
          },
          "body": "If the StopFilter constructor that takes in a Set no longer needs the \"boolean ignoreCase\" we should probably: deprecate that constructor, document that ignoreCase is ignoredand the Set must only contain lowercase items, add a new Set based constructor without that param.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=hossman",
            "name": "hossman",
            "key": "hossman",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=hossman&avatarId=21247"
            },
            "displayName": "Chris M. Hostetter",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Phoenix"
          },
          "created": "2007-11-01T02:25:33.427+0000",
          "updated": "2007-11-01T02:25:33.427+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12381579/comment/12539319",
          "id": "12539319",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "\nWoops, you're right, sorry about that, and thanks for fixing it Yonik!\n\nI made a few small changes to your patch (attached\nCharArraySet.take2.patch): there were some problems with rehashing, so\nI also added a new unit test (don't forget to \"svn add\" before\ncommitting!).  All tests pass.\n\nI noticed that in your patch you now assume that String.hashCode() is\nalways as described in Sun's javadocs, but that makes me a little\nnervous, eg:\n\n    http://forum.java.sun.com/thread.jspa?threadID=762602&messageID=4351604\n\nMaybe for the String case we should continue computing hashCode\nourselves?\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2007-11-01T09:41:00.230+0000",
          "updated": "2007-11-01T09:41:00.230+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12381579/comment/12539422",
          "id": "12539422",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "> I noticed that in your patch you now assume that String.hashCode() is always as described in Sun's javadocs\n\nThe fact that it's in their javadocs seems to make it part of the interface though.\nUsing String.hash (for cached strings - hashCode already calculated) resulted in a 15% lookup improvement.\n\nSide note: looking up char[] was faster in any event... probably because the extra bounds checking code for every String.charAt()\n\nOn the other hand... not being tied to String.hashCode() means we could select a faster method if we chose to do so.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
